Subject: [PATCH] SweetSurface: retain only state mappings in released-view cache

Released views keep state mappings for racing IOSurfaceClientGetSeed readers.
The mapping owns the state descriptor; retaining SweetSurface too pins retired
pixel allocations until up to 256 later releases in every client. Drop that
separate surface reference after dropping its table user count.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
@@ -1559,6 +1559,9 @@
 		 */
 		OSSafeReleaseNULL(ref->data);
 		sweet_surface_put(ref->surface);
+		/* The state mapping retains its descriptor independently. A zombie must
+		 * not retain the surface and its retired (often full-screen) pixels. */
+		OSSafeReleaseNULL(ref->surface);
 		ref->released = true;
 		ref->detached = false;
 		if (fZombies != NULL && fZombies->setObject(ref)) {
